{
  "statement": "The nightly pass keeps a thread's notes true for the member it runs as: duplicates fold, what belongs together combines, what has stopped being true is set aside, and the rest is left alone. It changes only that member's notes, never rewrites a person's words, never deletes what a person typed, and adds no knowledge the notes did not hold.",
  "why": "An assistant whose idea of you is append-only gets worse the longer you use it. But a person's correction beats an inference, so the only words that can be removed are ones offload wrote itself, and a day where nothing changes is a normal day.",
  "sources": [
    "014 AC-8, AC-9, AC-10, AC-10a, AC-13, AC-14a",
    "032 AC-8",
    "nightly.md",
    "nightly.py: listing, _held_to_the_rules"
  ],
  "cases": [
